From 4b48a3423a8a40bccbbecf3dc93faa92bedb1e56 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nic Boet <nic@boet.cc>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 22:35:57 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] feat(server): public_prefix for URLs written behind a proxy
 path

A reverse proxy can publish zm-api under a path, e.g. /zm/api/v3 next to
the rest of ZoneMinder, and strip it before passing requests on. Requests
then work, but URLs zm-api writes into responses still start at the site
root: live HLS master playlists, signed media links, the live-start
response, the WHEP session Location, search result URLs, and Swagger UI's
document URL and "try it out" target. A client following them leaves the
proxied path.

server.public_prefix (APP_SERVER__PUBLIC_PREFIX), empty by default, is
prepended to those URLs only. Routing, media grants and the zm-web
fallback keep the paths zm-api serves. With a prefix set, the OpenAPI
document gets it as its server URL and Swagger UI fetches the document
through it. Documented in base.toml, the packaged zm-api.env and
zm-api.env(5).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
